# macOS exported-symbols list for the static-link build of cpp_demo/test.
#
# Counterpart to paimon-export.ver (which is a GNU ld version script and only
# works with GNU ld / lld on Linux). Apple's ld64 uses a different mechanism:
#
#   clang ... -Wl,-exported_symbols_list,paimon-export.exp
#
# ld64 exports ONLY the symbols matched here and hides every other global
# symbol (the Rust runtime, zlib internals, and anything a vendored C dep
# drags in) from the executable's exported symbol table. This keeps the
# binary's ABI surface limited to the paimon C API, mirroring the Linux
# version-script behaviour.
#
# Note the leading underscore: C symbols get a `_` prefix in the Mach-O
# symbol table, so `paimon_open` becomes `_paimon_open`.
_paimon_*
